      {
        "id": 125968,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-09T21:00:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't think Andy's count for Vengeance is correct:</p>\n<blockquote>Vengeance &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 349&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;5 heroes: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 5 x 41 = 205 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;5 vengeance villains: &nbsp; 5 x 22 = 110&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;2 environments: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 2 x 15 = &nbsp;30&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Sentinels characters&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Fright Train &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 1&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Idealist &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 1&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Mainstay &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 1&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Writhe &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 1\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nThere were no normal-sized villain character cards, only oversized ones. &nbsp;So the count for the 5 Vengeance villains should be 100, not 110. &nbsp;However given that, my overall count somehow matches Andy's exactly, once you add one to his total for Kvothe (2094). &nbsp;Not sure how that happened.My count is in the front of my card list, which I'll be updating tonight.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>It's two wrongs making a right. I used 5x22=110 instead of 5x20=100, but then I also added 351 to 1,438 and got 1,779 (instead of 1,789).</p>\n<p>I think that somewhere along the way I'd realized the problem with 110 vs 100, but only fixed the running count and not the details.</p>",
